<bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference4525">
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref50607" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q8IXN7 RIMKLA</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RIMKLA</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FAM80A</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Catalyzes the synthesis of N-acetyl-L-aspartyl-L-glutamate (NAAG) and N-acetyl-L-aspartyl-L-glutamyl-L-glutamate.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY N-acetyl-L-aspartate + L-glutamate + ATP = N-acetyl-L-aspartyl-L-glutamate + ADP + phosphate + H(+)CATALYTIC ACTIVITY N-acetyl-L-aspartate + 2 L-glutamate + 2 ATP = N-acetyl-L-aspartyl-L-glutamyl-L-glutamate + 2 ADP + 2 phosphate + 2 H(+)COFACTOR Binds 2 magnesium or manganese ions per subunit.INTERACTION N-acetyl-L-aspartyl-L-glutamate (NAAG) is the most abundant dipeptide present in vertebrate central nervous system (CNS).SIMILARITY Belongs to the RimK family.SEQUENCE CAUTION Truncated N-terminus.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

